        "original_id": "35608110-0892-5767-a6c1-32538223356e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Tropicana Products, PepsiCo, Pepsi-Cola Company\n- Brands: Mountain Dew\n- People: Anthony T. Rossi\n- Places: Bradenton, Florida, United States, Canada\n- Topics: acquisitions, ownership, founding, expansion\n\nFacts:\n- Anthony T. Rossi was an Italian immigrant born on September 13, 1900, and he founded Tropicana Products in 1947 in Bradenton, Florida, in the United States.\n- Tropicana Products was founded as a producer of orange juice and later expanded into multiple product lines.\n- In August 1964, the Pepsi-Cola Company acquired the Mountain Dew brand and production rights from Tip.\n- After the August 1964 acquisition, Mountain Dew distribution expanded more widely across the United States and Canada.\n- Since 1998, Tropicana Products has been owned by PepsiCo.\n- Tropicana Products grew from 50 employees to over 8,000 in 2004 and became one of the world's largest producers and marketers of citrus juice.\n- Anthony T. Rossi died on January 24, 1993.",
